WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.837
Why now?

2
00:00:00.837 --> 00:00:04.050
Because two migrations
open one design window.

3
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:09.081
On the HR side, an OMB and OPM
memo creates Federal HR 2.0,

4
00:00:09.081 --> 00:00:12.625
one government-wide core HR platform.

5
00:00:12.625 --> 00:00:16.704
OPM awarded the platform
contract in June 2026,

6
00:00:16.704 --> 00:00:21.725
and the first agencies start
moving as fiscal 2027 begins.

7
00:00:21.725 --> 00:00:24.902
The sample timeline is about
eight months per agency,

8
00:00:24.902 --> 00:00:28.800
with the agency's interconnections
going live around month five.

9
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.152
On the identity side, agencies
are already moving to Entra ID,

10
00:00:33.152 --> 00:00:35.850
which Identity and Directory covers.

11
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.232
There, attributes drive Conditional
Access, groups and delegation,

12
00:00:40.232 --> 00:00:43.675
and feeding them from an HR
system is a supported path.

13
00:00:43.675 --> 00:00:48.260
So the window is this: design the
identity feed in during HR onboarding,

14
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:52.450
before those interconnections go
live, not bolted on afterward.

15
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:57.150
One honest limit: HR 2.0
covers federal employees only.

16
00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.181
Contractors need their
own authoritative source,

17
00:01:00.181 --> 00:01:03.260
and onboarding is the right
time to decide that too.
